From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3dx10_43, d3dx11_43: 1D and 3D textures (load, filter, copy, save) (3680)

d3dx10_43, d3dx11_43: 1D and 3D textures (load, filter, copy, save)

Loading a 1D image or DDS creates an ID3D10/11Texture1D (it was loaded as a
2D texture). Volumes get the same resize, format conversion and mip-chain
generation that 2D images have (box average over the covered slices; BC
volumes are decoded and re-encoded slice by slice, and the Depth member of
the load info is honoured). FilterTexture, LoadTextureFromTexture (with
source and destination boxes in all three axes) and SaveTextureToMemory now
work on 1D and 3D resources; 1D saves as a DDS or as a width x 1 image, a
volume saves as a DDS with the depth flag and the volume cap.
---
